  "prefLabel": "Sphc 102.08 Otolaryngologist",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Sphc 102.08 \"Otolaryngologist\" means “otolaryngologist” as defined in RSA 326-F:1, VI, namely, “a physician licensed in the state of New Hampshire who specializes in medical problems of the ear, nose, and throat, and is eligible for qualification by the American Board of Otolaryngology as an otolaryngologist.”\n\nSource. #14193, eff 2-12-25",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/sphc100.html"
}
